# Fact Knowledge Layer - optional configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (which is git-ignored) and edit. Nothing here is required: with
# no .env the system runs entirely locally on the default GGUF model.
#   cp env.example .env
# or run the helper:  ./scripts/setup-groq.sh
#
# A real environment variable always overrides the matching line here.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq - free, no credit card, ~100x faster than local CPU inference.
# Full corpus in seconds instead of an hour. Get a key (2 minutes):
#
#   1. Open https://console.groq.com  and sign in (Google/GitHub, no card).
#   2. Left sidebar -> "API Keys" -> "Create API Key". Name it anything.
#   3. Copy the key (starts with `gsk_`) - it is shown once.
#   4. Paste it below, uncomment both lines, save as .env
#   5. Check it took:  python run.py status   (backend line should say "groq")
#
# Free-tier limits are per-minute token/request caps, not a spend cap; the
# pipeline is resumable, so a rate-limit pause is harmless.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BACKEND=groq
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_replace_me

# Model used when LLM_BACKEND=groq (any Groq-hosted chat model).
# FKL_GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local backend tuning (only relevant when LLM_BACKEND is unset or "local")
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Force CPU even on a CUDA/Metal build (0), or cap offloaded layers (N).
# FKL_N_GPU_LAYERS=0

# Deterministic, no-model extraction - guarantees the pipeline runs anywhere.
# LLM_BACKEND=none
